The assessment is written and committed at session_plan/assessment.md. The build is green: the harness verified this commit, CI passed on the last 5 pushes, and the last 10 sessions each finished 2/2 tasks with no reverts.

What the probes found (binary 5ea96be3, run from an empty directory):
• Two commands exit 0 after failing, and no issue tracks them. yoyo ast <pattern> exits 0 when ast-grep isn't installed, and yoyo goal set with no description prints usage and exits 0. A script can't tell either apart from success. Last session named both in a comment on #1086 but didn't open an issue for them, and nothing since has fixed them.
• #1086 has 12 shell commands left that print in-session syntax (usage: /grep, /docs, /ast, /blame, and so on). def and outline were missing from the issue's list; I added them in a comment on #1086.
• A model id written with a dot gets the wrong settings without any warning. The settings lookup matches names by their beginning, so --model claude-opus-5.5 gets claude-opus-5's limits and price. Claude Code 2.1.314 fixed exactly this bug. I haven't checked whether any gateway yoyo supports actually sends dotted ids.
• Claude Code 2.1.314 can block file writes outside the working directories in every permission mode (blockWritesOutsideWorkingDirectories). yoyo asks before reading outside the launch directory, but its own docs say writes are "a different fence", left to --restricted and --allow-dir. I took this from the docs and code and didn't run it.
• One thing yoyo already gets right: a -p run that fails at startup (no key, unknown model) exits 1 with an error. Claude Code only just fixed that for itself.

I saved the Claude Code 2.1.314 comparison to yopedia. The assessment ends with four candidate tasks for the planner, in this order: the exit-code pair, the remaining #1086 commands, the dotted model id, and the outside-directory write fence.

